            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "A. Punctuality in reporting to the job is expected from every employee and is essential to the smooth operation of the business.",
            "block_bbox": [
                339,
                433,
                1448,
                495
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    339.0,
                    433.0
                ],
                [
                    1448.0,
                    433.0
                ],
                [
                    1448.0,
                    495.0
                ],
                [
                    339.0,
                    495.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "B. 1. An absence occurs any time an employee is scheduled to work, but does not report. This does NOT include approved time off for vacation, holidays, bereavement leave, jury duty, approved leave of absence including pre-approved sick leave, or for any other written approved reason. All employees who are unable to report to work must inform the personnel office prior to their scheduled starting time and inform them of the reason for their pending absence, and how long they will be out An employee out of work due to illness for five (5) or more working days must provide Human Resources, for purposes of SDI, current medical certification of ability to work, or inability to work. In cases of Worker's Compensation, this certification must still be provided on the first day.",
            "block_bbox": [
                340,
                518,
                1481,
                750
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 9,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    340.0,
                    518.0
                ],
                [
                    1481.0,
                    518.0
                ],
                [
                    1481.0,
                    750.0
                ],
                [
                    340.0,
                    750.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "2. The Employer shall consider all circumstances presented by an employee (or union representative on his behalf) before classifying an attendance incident as an “occurrence” or “irregularity”.",
            "block_bbox": [
                341,
                774,
                1468,
                835
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 10,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    341.0,
                    774.0
                ],
